-- What the core 3rd-level spells do, in a sentence or three of our own words. Shown
-- in place of the bare facts a spell's entry is built from (see Data/SpellSummaries.lua).
local _, ns = ...
local R = ns.Rules

R.SPELL_SUMMARIES = R.SPELL_SUMMARIES or {}
local S = R.SPELL_SUMMARIES

S["Animate Dead"] = "Takes a minute. Bones or a corpse of a Small or Medium humanoid within 10 feet rise as a skeleton or zombie that obeys you for 24 hours; a bonus action commands those within 60 feet. Cast it again to keep control of up to four. Two more undead for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Aura of Vitality"] = "For up to a minute, when you cast it and at the start of each of your turns, you restore 2d6 hit points to one creature within 30 feet of you."
S["Beacon of Hope"] = "For up to a minute the creatures you choose within 30 feet have advantage on Wisdom saves and death saves, and any healing they receive restores the most it can."
S["Bestow Curse"] = "A creature you touch that fails a Wisdom save is cursed for up to a minute, in one way you pick: disadvantage with one ability, disadvantage on attacks against you, a Wisdom save each turn or it can only dodge, or 1d8 extra necrotic damage from your attacks and spells. Higher slots last longer, without concentration from 5th."
S["Blinding Smite"] = "Bonus action right after you hit with a melee weapon or unarmed strike: 3d8 extra radiant damage and the target is blinded for a minute. It makes a Constitution save at the end of each of its turns to end it. 1d8 more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Blink"] = "For a minute, roll a d6 at the end of each of your turns: on 4 to 6 you slip into the Ethereal Plane, out of reach, and return at the start of your next turn within 10 feet of where you left."
S["Call Lightning"] = "A storm cloud forms overhead within 120 feet for up to 10 minutes. When you cast it, and with an action on later turns, a bolt strikes a point under the cloud: creatures within 5 feet take 3d10 lightning damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. 1d10 more if you cast it outdoors in a storm, and for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Clairvoyance"] = "Takes 10 minutes. An invisible sensor appears in a place you know, or an obvious one, within a mile. For up to 10 minutes you see or hear through it, switching with a bonus action."
S["Conjure Animals"] = "A spectral pack appears within 60 feet for up to 10 minutes and moves 30 feet when you move. A creature the pack comes within 10 feet of, or that enters that space or ends its turn there, takes 3d10 slashing damage unless it passes a Dexterity save. Near the pack you have advantage on Strength saves. 1d10 more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Conjure Barrage"] = "Spectral weapons fly out in a 60-foot cone: the creatures you choose take 5d8 force damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. 1d8 more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Counterspell"] = "Reaction when a creature within 60 feet casts a spell: it makes a Constitution save. If it fails, the spell fizzles and its action is wasted, though the spell slot is not spent."
S["Create Food and Water"] = "You create 45 pounds of plain food and 30 gallons of clean water within 30 feet. The food spoils after a day."
S["Crusader's Mantle"] = "For up to a minute, you and your allies within 30 feet of you deal 1d4 extra radiant damage on each hit with a weapon or unarmed strike."
S["Daylight"] = "Sunlight fills a 60-foot sphere within 60 feet, or spreads from an object you cast it on, for an hour, with dim light 60 feet beyond. It dispels magical darkness of 3rd level or lower that it touches."
S["Dispel Magic"] = "Ends every spell of 3rd level or lower on a creature, object or effect within 120 feet. For each higher one, roll a spellcasting ability check against 10 plus its level. A higher slot ends spells up to its own level without a roll."
S["Elemental Weapon"] = "For up to an hour a nonmagical weapon you touch has +1 to attack rolls and deals 1d4 extra acid, cold, fire, lightning or thunder damage. +2 and 2d4 with a 5th or 6th-level slot, +3 and 3d4 with 7th or higher."
S["Fear"] = "Creatures in a 30-foot cone that fail a Wisdom save drop what they hold and are frightened for up to a minute, dashing away from you each turn. One that ends its turn out of your sight saves again."
S["Feign Death"] = "A willing creature you touch appears dead for an hour, even to magic. It is blinded and incapacitated and can't move, but resists all damage except psychic and can't be poisoned."
S["Fireball"] = "An explosion in a 20-foot sphere within 150 feet: 8d6 fire damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. It sets loose flammable objects alight. 1d6 more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Fly"] = "A willing creature you touch has a fly speed of 60 feet and can hover for up to 10 minutes. It falls if still in the air when the spell ends. One more target for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Gaseous Form"] = "A willing creature you touch becomes a cloud of mist for up to an hour: it flies at 10 feet, slips through cracks, resists bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage, and can't attack or cast spells. One more target for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Glyph of Warding"] = "Takes an hour. You inscribe a hidden glyph on a surface or inside an object, with a trigger you set. It either explodes in a 20-foot sphere for 5d8 damage of a type you pick, half on a successful Dexterity save, or releases a spell of 3rd level or lower you stored in it. 1d8 more, or a higher stored spell, for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Haste"] = "A willing creature within 30 feet has double speed, +2 Armor Class, advantage on Dexterity saves and one extra limited action each turn, for up to a minute. When it ends the target can't move or act until the end of its next turn."
S["Hunger of Hadar"] = "A 20-foot sphere of utter darkness opens within 150 feet for up to a minute: difficult terrain, and creatures inside are blinded. Starting a turn there deals 2d6 cold damage; ending one there deals 2d6 acid damage unless the creature passes a Dexterity save. 1d6 more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Hypnotic Pattern"] = "Creatures in a 30-foot cube within 120 feet that see the pattern and fail a Wisdom save are charmed for up to a minute: incapacitated and unable to move. Damage, or another creature's action to shake it, ends it for that creature."
S["Leomund's Tiny Hut"] = "Takes a minute. A dome 10 feet around you stands for 8 hours. Those inside when you cast it come and go freely; nothing else gets in, nor do spells of 3rd level or lower. It ends if you leave."
S["Lightning Arrow"] = "Bonus action as your ranged attack hits or misses: in place of its normal damage the target takes 4d8 lightning damage, half on a miss. Creatures within 10 feet of it take 2d8, half on a successful Dexterity save. 1d8 more to both for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Lightning Bolt"] = "A bolt in a line 100 feet long and 5 feet wide from you: 8d6 lightning damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. 1d6 more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Magic Circle"] = "Takes a minute. A circle 10 feet in radius within 10 feet wards against celestials, elementals, fey, fiends or undead for an hour: they can't walk in, have disadvantage on attacks against those inside, and can't charm, frighten or possess them. It can be turned around to hold them in. An hour more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Major Image"] = "An illusion of anything up to a 20-foot cube appears within 120 feet for up to 10 minutes, with sound, smell and temperature. An action moves it. Touch passes through it, and an Investigation check against your spell save DC sees through it. With a 4th-level slot or higher it lasts until dispelled."
S["Mass Healing Word"] = "Bonus action. Up to six creatures you can see within 60 feet regain 2d4 hit points plus your spellcasting modifier. 1d4 more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Meld into Stone"] = "You step into stone large enough to hold you and stay hidden inside for up to 8 hours. You can't see out and hear poorly. Being forced out by damage to the stone hurts you."
S["Nondetection"] = "For 8 hours a willing creature, or a place or object up to 10 feet across, that you touch can't be targeted by divination spells or seen through scrying."
S["Phantom Steed"] = "Takes a minute. A saddled, horse-like mount appears within 30 feet for an hour, for you or a rider you choose. It moves 100 feet a round, 13 miles an hour, and fades if it takes any damage."
S["Plant Growth"] = "As an action, plants in a 100-foot radius within 150 feet grow so thick that every foot moved there costs 4. Cast over 8 hours instead, plants within half a mile yield twice the food for a year."
S["Protection from Energy"] = "For up to an hour a willing creature you touch resists one damage type you choose: acid, cold, fire, lightning or thunder."
S["Remove Curse"] = "Your touch ends every curse on a creature or object. A cursed magic item stays cursed, but its owner's attunement breaks so it can be put aside."
S["Revivify"] = "A creature you touch that died within the last minute returns to life with 1 hit point. It doesn't work on death from old age and restores no lost body parts."
S["Sending"] = "You send up to 25 words to a creature you have met or had described to you, at any distance, and it can reply at once in the same way. Across planes there is a small chance the message is lost."
S["Sleet Storm"] = "Sleet falls in a 20-foot radius within 150 feet for up to a minute: heavily obscured, difficult terrain. A creature that enters or starts its turn there must pass a Dexterity save or fall prone and lose concentration."
S["Slow"] = "Up to six creatures in a 40-foot cube within 120 feet that fail a Wisdom save are slowed for up to a minute: half speed, -2 to Armor Class and Dexterity saves, no reactions, and only an action or a bonus action each turn with a single attack. They save again at the end of each of their turns."
S["Speak with Dead"] = "A corpse within 10 feet that still has a mouth answers up to five questions over 10 minutes. It knows only what it knew in life, answers briefly, and need not tell the truth. It can't be asked again for 10 days."
S["Speak with Plants"] = "For 10 minutes the plants within 30 feet of where you cast it can talk with you about the past day and follow simple commands. You can turn overgrowth into easy ground, or easy ground into difficult terrain."
S["Spirit Guardians"] = "Spirits circle 15 feet around you for up to 10 minutes. Creatures you didn't exempt move at half speed there, and one that the aura reaches, or that enters it or ends its turn there, takes 3d8 radiant or necrotic damage, half on a successful Wisdom save, once per turn. 1d8 more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Stinking Cloud"] = "Foul gas fills a 20-foot sphere within 90 feet for up to a minute, heavily obscured. A creature that starts its turn there must pass a Constitution save or be poisoned for that turn and unable to take an action or bonus action."
S["Summon Fey"] = "A fey spirit in a fuming, mirthful or tricksy mood appears within 90 feet and fights for you for up to an hour, acting right after your turn on your spoken commands. A higher slot makes it stronger."
S["Summon Undead"] = "An undead spirit, ghostly, putrid or skeletal, appears within 90 feet and fights for you for up to an hour, acting right after your turn on your spoken commands. A higher slot makes it stronger."
S["Tongues"] = "For an hour a creature you touch understands every language it hears or sees signed, and anyone who knows a language understands what it says."
S["Vampiric Touch"] = "A melee spell attack for 3d6 necrotic damage; you regain half the damage dealt. For up to a minute you can make the attack again as an action. 1d6 more for each slot level above 3rd."
S["Water Breathing"] = "Up to ten willing creatures within 30 feet can breathe underwater for 24 hours, as well as breathing normally."
S["Water Walk"] = "Up to ten willing creatures within 30 feet can walk on water, mud, snow, acid or lava as if it were solid ground for an hour."
S["Wind Wall"] = "A wall of wind up to 50 feet long and 15 feet high rises within 120 feet for up to a minute. Creatures in it when it appears take 4d8 bludgeoning damage, half on a successful Strength save. Arrows, gases and small flying creatures can't get through."
